/// #2065 wall 1: a spawn-free `TaskGroup::run` under an injected Async entry
/// boundary.
///
/// `TaskGroup::run[T, rg, e](body: (TaskGroup[rg, e]) -> T with e)` takes its
/// body under a row VARIABLE, so the evidence pass withheld it and refused the
/// whole program ("type-directed evidence ... cannot see through
/// `TaskGroup::run`"). The body here is a closure literal that cannot perform
/// `Async`, which the call-site argument-inertness rule (queries.vibe,
/// `edp_argcond_admits`) admits; the program answers 42.
///
/// This is the first of the walls #2065 lists. A body that spawns a
/// suspend-class task under the same entry is wall 2
/// (fixtures/async_boundary_spawn_suspend_test.vibe).
import @vibe/concurrent {
  TaskGroup
}

fn main() -> Int allows Async + Exception {
  sleep(1)
  TaskGroup::run((g) -> {
    42
  })
}
